    "reasoningTemplate": "Subacute anaemia with neurological signs — sensory ataxia, dorsal-column/pyramidal deficits and cognitive/behavioural change — points to B12 (cobalamin) deficiency with subacute combined degeneration; often autoimmune (pernicious anaemia)."
  },
  "redFlags": [
    "Neurological damage may be irreversible if untreated — do not delay B12 replacement for a haematological response",
    "Do NOT give folate alone (can precipitate/worsen neurological deterioration)",
    "Check for pernicious anaemia (intrinsic-factor antibodies) and other autoimmune disease"
  ],
